{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 17:48:24.102515", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content='Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### Network Description\\nThe network consists of:\\n- **Hosts**: `pc1` (195.11.14.2) and `pc2` (200.1.1.2)\\n- **Routers**: `router1` and `router2` running FRRRouting\\n- **Topology**:\\n  - `router1:eth0` connected to `router2:eth0`\\n  - `router1:eth1` connected to `pc1:eth0`\\n  - `router2:eth1` connected to `pc2:eth0`\\n\\n#### Observations\\n1. **Reachability Tests**:\\n   - Ping tests between `pc1` and `pc2` failed:\\n     - From `pc1` to `pc2`: \"Network is unreachable.\"\\n     - From `pc2` to `pc1`: \"Destination Net Unreachable.\"\\n   - This indicates a lack of connectivity between the hosts.\\n\\n2. **Router Configuration Access**:\\n   - Attempts to retrieve BGP and IP routing configurations from `router1` and `router2` failed due to the absence of the `vtysh` command. This suggests that FRRRouting may not be properly configured or accessible.\\n\\n3. **Host Network Configurations**:\\n   - **pc1**:\\n     - IP: `195.11.14.2/24`\\n     - Default route: None\\n     - Interface `eth0` is up and running.\\n   - **pc2**:\\n     - IP: `200.1.1.2/24`\\n     - Default route: `200.1.1.1` via `eth0`\\n     - Interface `eth0` is up and running.\\n   - **router1**:\\n     - `eth0`: `193.10.11.1/24`\\n     - `eth1`: `195.11.14.1/24`\\n     - Routes:\\n       - `193.10.11.0/24` via `eth0`\\n       - `195.11.14.0/24` via `eth1`\\n   - **router2**:\\n     - `eth0`: `193.10.11.2/24`\\n     - `eth1`: `200.1.1.1/24`\\n     - Routes:\\n       - `193.10.11.0/24` via `eth0`\\n       - `200.1.1.0/24` via `eth1`\\n\\n#### Findings\\n1. **Routing Issues**:\\n   - `pc1` lacks a default route, preventing it from reaching `pc2`.\\n   - `router1` and `router2` have no routes to each other\\'s subnets (`195.11.14.0/24` and `200.1.1.0/24`), indicating a potential BGP misconfiguration.\\n\\n2. **BGP Configuration**:\\n   - Unable to retrieve BGP configurations from the routers due to missing `vtysh`. This raises concerns about the operational state of FRRRouting.\\n\\n3. **Connectivity**:\\n   - The direct link between `router1:eth0` and `router2:eth0` appears functional based on interface states, but routing issues prevent communication between subnets.\\n\\n#### Conclusion\\nThe network is experiencing significant connectivity issues due to routing misconfigurations and potential BGP setup problems. Further investigation into the routers\\' BGP configurations and operational state is required to identify the root cause., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='0b8175c5-81f6-4bd0-bd61-247a9c81ccbf'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
